+## 🎯 Project Overview
+
+Pulseboard is a small browser-based product for team facilitators who lose follow-through after weekly meetings. A facilitator uploads a meeting transcript, reviews proposed action items, and must explicitly confirm an owner and due date before an item can enter the reminder workflow. It turns a noisy meeting record into accountable commitments without becoming a meeting recorder, calendar replacement, or autonomous messaging system. The pilot matters now because five teams can test whether the confirmation gate produces a measurable drop in unowned overdue actions.
+
+## 🎨 Project Type & Scale
+
+**Type**: Web Application (browser-based, responsive)
+
+**Estimated Scale**: Level 2 — a focused pilot product with one core workflow and several bounded capability areas; planning will refine the story count.
+
+**Primary Domain**: Enterprise/B2B — team operations and meeting follow-through.
+
+**Project archetype**: `b2b_saas`.
+
+**Domain Expertise Required**: No. The product has operational workflow concerns, but the brief supplies the governing business rules; no specialized regulated-domain model is implied.
+
+## Vision & Goals
+
+### Vision Statement
+
+A world where team facilitators turn every weekly-meeting commitment into an owned, dated action so that important work does not quietly become overdue and orphaned.
+
+### Primary Goals
+
+1. **Review adoption**: Have facilitators review at least 80% of proposed action items during the five-team pilot.
+   - Success looks like: proposed items do not linger unexamined after transcript upload.
+   - Key metric: reviewed proposed items ÷ all proposed items in the pilot.
+
+2. **Accountability quality**: Reduce unowned overdue actions by 30% after four weeks.
+   - Success looks like: fewer overdue commitments lack a named person responsible for them.
+   - Key metric: count of overdue action items without an owner, compared with the pilot baseline measured before rollout.
+
+3. **Safe commitment creation**: Prevent a reminder from being scheduled until a facilitator confirms both an owner and a due date.
+   - Success looks like: every scheduled reminder is backed by an explicit human decision.
+   - Key metric: zero scheduled reminders missing either confirmed field.
+
+4. **Pilot fit**: Support a usable, repeatable workflow for five teams' weekly meetings.
+   - Success looks like: each pilot team can move from transcript to reviewed actions without relying on a separate meeting-recording or calendar product.
+   - Key metric: participating teams completing the workflow in their normal weekly-meeting cadence.
+
